WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.539 --> 00:00:07.160
OK, so we already looked at Steve Scalise
turning a question about Marjorie Taylor Green's

00:00:07.160 --> 00:00:12.370
outrageous comments into an answer about China,
Joe Biden and carbon.

00:00:12.370 --> 00:00:15.809
Let's now go to our second example of the
day.

00:00:15.809 --> 00:00:22.040
This is Republican Congresswoman Nancy Mace
asked on Fox News about the ludicrous things

00:00:22.040 --> 00:00:24.279
that Marjorie Taylor Green has said.

00:00:24.279 --> 00:00:29.730
Remember, we've uncovered videos of Marjorie
Taylor Green talking about Jewish space lasers

00:00:29.730 --> 00:00:32.410
as the cause for California wildfires.

00:00:32.410 --> 00:00:36.480
Marjorie Taylor Green being a 9/11 denier.

00:00:36.480 --> 00:00:42.000
Marjorie Taylor Green talking about political
violence as a good thing, as something that

00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:44.460
that needs to be done on and on and on.

00:00:44.460 --> 00:00:45.910
Republicans are being asked to comment.

00:00:45.910 --> 00:00:49.970
Nancy Mace is a Republican congresswoman from
South Carolina.

00:00:49.970 --> 00:00:57.630
Some believed not me, but some believed that
she was a more moderate, rational voice in

00:00:57.630 --> 00:00:59.180
the Republican Party.

00:00:59.180 --> 00:01:00.850
She went on Fox News yesterday.

00:01:00.850 --> 00:01:05.791
She was asked about Marjorie Taylor Green's
comments and she actually to her credit, she

00:01:05.791 --> 00:01:12.490
seemed to concede that Marjorie Taylor Green
is crazy, but she played the both sides game

00:01:12.490 --> 00:01:17.570
saying there are crazy people on both sides
and then gave a number of false equivalency.

00:01:17.570 --> 00:01:18.810
So let's take a look.

00:01:18.810 --> 00:01:20.920
There are crazies on both sides of the aisle.

00:01:20.920 --> 00:01:22.450
We've seen that.

00:01:22.450 --> 00:01:26.100
You know, it's not just Republicans that have
our own issues where Democrats have them,

00:01:26.100 --> 00:01:27.100
too.

00:01:27.100 --> 00:01:31.740
We've seen Maxine Waters tell folks to go
and threaten and harm members of the Trump

00:01:31.740 --> 00:01:32.740
administration.

00:01:32.740 --> 00:01:33.740
Right.

00:01:33.740 --> 00:01:35.409
We've seen crazies on both sides of the aisle.

00:01:35.409 --> 00:01:37.659
We do have to, I think, address some of these
issues.

00:01:37.659 --> 00:01:40.400
But, you know, some of these things and I'm
learning about them today.

00:01:40.400 --> 00:01:45.159
And this week, two were said before she was
elected and Georgia voters still elected her.

00:01:45.159 --> 00:01:50.150
Just a few years ago, we saw Democrat, another
Democrat from Georgia, Cynthia McKinney, assault

00:01:50.150 --> 00:01:51.510
a Capitol Hill police officer.

00:01:51.510 --> 00:01:53.310
And nothing was done after that either.

00:01:53.310 --> 00:01:54.400
So we've got to look at precedent.

00:01:54.400 --> 00:01:56.270
We've got to have this conversation.

00:01:56.270 --> 00:01:57.270
We have to address it.

00:01:57.270 --> 00:02:02.030
And if we do a better job of holding ourselves
accountable, we can also hold the left accountable

00:02:02.030 --> 00:02:03.030
as well.

00:02:03.030 --> 00:02:06.470
We have to have that moral authority and that
means addressing some of these situations.

00:02:06.470 --> 00:02:12.819
So, listen, if you if you need me to find
something positive about that, she does seem

00:02:12.819 --> 00:02:16.620
to be saying that Marjorie Taylor Green is
crazy.

00:02:16.620 --> 00:02:22.849
She is drawing false equivalencies to Maxine
Waters, though, and also saying this stuff

00:02:22.849 --> 00:02:28.109
was said before Marjorie Green was elected
is not particularly relevant.

00:02:28.109 --> 00:02:29.230
This is gaslighting.

00:02:29.230 --> 00:02:33.629
This is what about ISM two side stuff and
it's a complete farce.

00:02:33.629 --> 00:02:37.269
And at least she's admitting Marjorie Taylor
Green is crazy.

00:02:37.269 --> 00:02:43.499
But Maxine Waters never followed around an
18 year old kid that was at a school during

00:02:43.499 --> 00:02:48.980
a school shooting accusing that kid of wanting
to take her guns away, as Marjorie Taylor

00:02:48.980 --> 00:02:50.840
Green did to David Hogg.

00:02:50.840 --> 00:02:56.480
Maxine Waters never said that there were wild
fires started by, I don't know, Catholic space

00:02:56.480 --> 00:02:58.639
lasers or anything like that.

00:02:58.639 --> 00:03:03.969
And by the way, even if these examples from
the other side were equivalent there in the

00:03:03.969 --> 00:03:10.709
past and they have nothing to do with Nancy
Mace and Republicans now dealing with Marjorie

00:03:10.709 --> 00:03:17.760
Taylor Green, who is in her own party at this
point in time, Nancy Mace actually has a sort

00:03:17.760 --> 00:03:20.230
of clever approach to a lot of these interviews.

00:03:20.230 --> 00:03:23.900
I've seen other interviews where when Nancy
is asked what you would think or questions

00:03:23.900 --> 00:03:28.909
she really has to answer, she'll sort of fast
talk through a bunch of distortions and lies.

00:03:28.909 --> 00:03:31.079
It's sort of a Gish Gallop technique.

00:03:31.079 --> 00:03:35.379
And very often anchors are interviewers even
either don't have the wherewithal or skill

00:03:35.379 --> 00:03:40.239
to point it out or just don't have the time
because a lot of these segments last four

00:03:40.239 --> 00:03:41.239
minutes.

00:03:41.239 --> 00:03:43.859
It's hard to refute six lies in four minutes.

00:03:43.859 --> 00:03:46.650
And Nancy Mace used very similar.

00:03:46.650 --> 00:03:52.639
Talking points on CNN over the weekend, they
are terrible talking points, but she is getting

00:03:52.639 --> 00:03:54.529
away with them.

00:03:54.529 --> 00:03:56.019
And as I said before.

00:03:56.019 --> 00:04:02.840
I am disgusted that Republicans, even with
these people, aren't just straight up calling

00:04:02.840 --> 00:04:07.049
them out and saying there's no room for this
insanity in the Republican Party, obviously

00:04:07.049 --> 00:04:09.099
it's disappointing they're not doing that.

00:04:09.099 --> 00:04:11.519
I'm not surprised that they're not doing it.

00:04:11.519 --> 00:04:17.060
But there is a political calculation happening
here where to some degree, I think they believe

00:04:17.060 --> 00:04:23.480
the further they get from January 6th, the
further they get from Trump being in office,

00:04:23.480 --> 00:04:27.470
the more they can kind of just shut their
mouths about these people and claim that they're

00:04:27.470 --> 00:04:32.130
about legislation and they're about stopping
socialism and government takeover of health

00:04:32.130 --> 00:04:37.280
care and reducing the deficit, all that stuff
that they pretend to care about and just sort

00:04:37.280 --> 00:04:41.620
of not comment on people like Marjorie Taylor
Green, Lauren, Bobert, Madison, Cawthorn and

00:04:41.620 --> 00:04:42.620
others.

00:04:42.620 --> 00:04:47.940
So ultimately, I believe that the test as
to whether these radical new members of Congress

00:04:47.940 --> 00:04:53.920
will become a significant part of the Republican
Party will be whether they get reelected in

00:04:53.920 --> 00:04:55.020
2022.

00:04:55.020 --> 00:05:02.540
Democrats do have a path to expelling these
folks from committee assignments, but it would

00:05:02.540 --> 00:05:06.630
take Republicans to really be able to get
them out of the House of Representatives.

00:05:06.630 --> 00:05:08.420
I don't expect that to happen.

00:05:08.420 --> 00:05:12.030
We talked on the bonus show yesterday about
how there have only been five expulsions in

00:05:12.030 --> 00:05:13.760
the history of the house.

00:05:13.760 --> 00:05:18.650
Three of them were in the eighteen hundreds
against members who were straight up supporting

00:05:18.650 --> 00:05:19.990
the Confederacy.

00:05:19.990 --> 00:05:24.320
The other two were in the 20th century, was
one of them in the 21st.

00:05:24.320 --> 00:05:28.810
The other two were in the modern political
era and they were four members of Congress

00:05:28.810 --> 00:05:30.750
who had actually been convicted of crimes.

00:05:30.750 --> 00:05:35.580
And so I am not optimistic at all that we
are going to see these folks expelled.

00:05:35.580 --> 00:05:39.020
Of course, it says a lot about the Republican
Party that they're unwilling to really take

00:05:39.020 --> 00:05:40.580
a stand against them.

00:05:40.580 --> 00:05:42.990
But that's not particularly surprising to
me.

00:05:42.990 --> 00:05:47.400
I'd be shocked if it were to you if you've
been paying attention to what has happened

00:05:47.400 --> 00:05:52.760
to the Republican Party, even casually over
the last few years.

00:05:52.760 --> 00:05:54.190
We will take a quick break.

00:05:54.190 --> 00:05:57.160
Much more coming up in just moments.

